    "taxonId": 55193,
    "summary": "A slow-growing, long-lived evergreen conifer endemic to California’s coastal ranges and Sierra Nevada foothills. It has stiff, sharp needles and large nut-like seeds enclosed in fleshy coverings that turn dark green to purple in late autumn. In deep shade it may lean or develop several stems, and it can resprout slowly after fire or other disturbance.",
    "humanEdibility": "yes",
    "edibilityNote": "The seeds were reportedly highly valued as food by Indigenous Californians, but are inedible raw.",
